From 8f791ce2baefa4c356fe4efb1311b0be3e56335c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy <andylee77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:09:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] cameras: UVision MC-A85 / Anpviz IPC-D3B83B-S
 (yma85_ssc378_gc8613, 4K)

SSC378DE + GC8613, 2560x1440 + 1280x720, scaled from the sensor's full
3840x2160 readout, which leaves far more of the video-memory heap free than a
4K main (3840x2160 stays a choice in the web UI): its own board DTS, the
GC8613 built from source, FlickerEx anti-flicker, luma day/night with the IR
ladder, the mic. It boots under the stock OEM U-Boot and flash layout, with the U-Boot
env kept in a file. The RAPTOR_* keys are in raptor.config. The OEM sensor
tuning (gc8613.bin) is a vendor file and is not included.
